# Trust and claims

> The interface must never appear more mature by pretending. It should appear more mature by being unusually clear, complete, and considered.

Register every customer-facing claim in `.cursor/experience-memory/trust-evidence-register.md` with evidence and verification source.

## Prohibited

- Fabricated testimonials, customer logos, or activity feeds
- Fake live counters or manufactured scarcity
- Unsupported "enterprise-grade," "SOC 2 compliant," or security badges unless verified
- Invented performance benchmarks
- Misleading comparison tables
- Visual implication that unavailable features are live
- Fake demo output presented as live capability
- Inaccurate integration status ("Works with X" when not shipped)

## Required honesty

- Product claims match shipped functionality
- Metrics verifiable or labeled as examples
- Screenshots reflect real or clearly labeled demo UI
- Pricing, renewal, trial, and refund terms clear
- Security and privacy language accurate (`legal-drafting.mdc` for policies)
- Company identity accurate per `company.mdc`
- Contact information real

## Build trust through

- Product transparency and visible functionality
- Clear system behavior and thoughtful errors
- Specific explanations over vague reassurance
- Real demonstrations (`interactive-demo-engineer`)
- Coherent legal and support surfaces
- Professional billing behavior
- Honest status communication

## Invoke

`trust-experience-designer` when adding pricing, signup, checkout, security pages, integrations, AI behavior explanations, or marketing proof.

Update `trust-evidence-register.md` for every new claim.
